Introduction
In
Part 1
we argued that Expert Advisors drift away from the strategies that inspired them because developers start coding before they understand how their own rules behave. Instead of writing the EA first, we built a logger that watched the market and recorded what the strategy would have seen without ever placing a trade. We ran it on GBPUSD M15 during the Tokyo session from January 2025 through August 2026. It produced 419 fully measured breakout events. Each event had 61 columns: 39 known at breakout time and 22 available only in hindsight.
The nine analysis phases contradicted most of our assumptions. Volume confirmation did not separate winners from losers in this dataset. Breakout candle size, range size, ATR level, and time of day were similarly inert. Most signal came from two features:
range location relative to prior-day structure on the breakout side, and breakout candle body cleanliness. The strongest separators—retest depth and whether the retest held—were post-entry by construction, so they are useful for management but not for selection. In this article we are turning that evidence into working code. We continue the same conversation with the MetaTrader 5 AI Assistant where Phase 9 left off, carry it through three more phases, and then write the Expert Advisor.
From Analysis to Logic
Phases 1 through 9 were descriptive. Every one of them ended with an instruction not to produce trading rules, because the point was to understand the strategy rather than to justify a conclusion we had already reached. The next three phases finally cross that line, but they cross it carefully: first the entry, then the exits, then a deliberate attempt to break what we just built.
Phase 10: Establishing the entry logic
Goal:
Propose a complete entry logic using only the features classified as safe for entry decisions, with thresholds, direction scope, and whether each condition is a hard gate or a preference weight.
Output:
Condition
Threshold
Scope
Classification
Distance to prior-day structure, breakout side
≤ +50 pts; core ≤ 0; exclusion > +400
Both
Hard gate plus hard exclusion
Breakout candle body ratio
≥ 0.79
Both
