One detail here deserves to be stated plainly, because it is the kind of thing that quietly invalidates a study. The Phase 10 proposal described the location gate as measuring from the breakout price, but the feature actually recorded in the dataset—and therefore the feature that produced the 54.5% success and 9.1% failure figures—is measured from the range edge. Those are different numbers, and the breakout price is always further past the level than the edge is. The code implements the range-edge version, because implementing the other one would mean testing a rule the evidence never evaluated.
The sign convention follows the logger. A positive distance means the range still has headroom before reaching the prior-day level on the breakout side; a negative distance means the range has already taken that level out. Winners clustered at a median of −39 points and failures at +330, so the gate admits ranges that sit at or past prior structure and rejects those floating in empty interior structure. The two things about it are worth stating. The +400 exclusion cannot change a decision-anything above +50 is already rejected—and exits only so the journal can separate "outside the zone" from "nowhere near structure". And the gate has no lower bound: a range that has taken the prior-day level out by any distance is admitted, a case the dataset never examined on its own.
The second gate is deliberately measuring decisiveness rather than magnitude. Phase 6 found candle size, in both raw points and ATR units, to be worthless as a separator, while body ratio widened the gap at every quartile. Counting the rejections separately in 'g_rejDist,'' 'g_rejExcl,' and 'g_rejBody' costs almost nothing and means the end-of-run summary can tell us which gate is doing the filtering—information that matters if the EA ever stops trading entirely. One qualification on the suspended confirmation. With InpUseDistATR switched on, the 0.25 ATR veto rejects the trade outright. That makes it a hard gate, not the preference weight Phase 10 recommended; only the 0.50 ATR upgrade behaves as a weight. We kept it as an experimental switch, and it is off in every backtest in this article, so it has no effect on the results shown. Separately, the 0.05 ATR buffer in the breakout test is itself a minimum penetration requirement, but it is the same tolerance the logger used when recording the data rather than a new filter.
Timing as a weight
