Phase 9 concluded that time deserves preference grading rather than hard filters, and this function is what that conclusion looks like in code. The contested 7-to-14 bar zone, with its 60% failure rate, gets 40% of normal size; the 3-to-6 bar anchor gets full size; the edges get 60%. A trade in a bad time window still happens, but it risks less, which is a genuinely different behavior from blocking it and is the one the evidence supports.
The three-way policy enum exists because a single sample of roughly twelve events per bucket is not strong enough to settle the question. 'TIME_OFF' gives the baseline, 'TIME_WEIGHT' applies the preference, and 'TIME_GATE' tests the hard block. Building all three in costs a dozen lines and means the question can be answered later with data rather than argued about now.
